title: Paralysis
subtitle: The economy seizes; the Assembly deadlocks...
new-page: true
on-arrival: paralysis_seen = 1; economic_growth -= 1; budget -= 1; dues -= 1 if dues > 2; disfavored += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 2; crisis_urgency += 1;
tags: event
view-if: veran_crash_seen = 1 and time >= crisis_start_time + 1
max-visits: 1
priority: 1

= Paralysis

The crash has become a general paralysis. Workshops stand idle, the great houses of the Guilds refuse to lend, and the Assembly is deadlocked, with each bench blaming the others while conditions worsen. Every month without action drives more of the unemployed toward the parties that promise to tear down the whole arrangement and start again.

Something must be done. The question is what.

- @lobby_dufour
- @appeal_calm
- @prepare_instability
- @emergency_controls

@lobby_dufour
title: Lobby President DuFour to act.
subtitle: Press the President to use the powers of his office.
on-arrival: crisis_urgency += 1; dufour_angry += 5; army_strength += 10; army_militancy += 0.05 if army_militancy < 8

We petition the President directly and urge him to act while the Assembly argues. DuFour receives our delegation coldly. He does not care to be lectured on his duties by the party that spent a decade restricting them, but he takes the point. Part of what he authorises goes to the army, since a government that fears disorder funds its soldiers before anything else. His opinion of us falls.

@appeal_calm
title: Appeal for calm.
subtitle: -1 resources. Reassure our coalition partners and the public.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if marcher_in_government and coalition_dissent > 0; gold_relation += 4*(1-dissent); lvp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); unionist_relation += 4*(1-dissent)

We spend the party's resources on reassurance rather than agitation: joint statements with our partners, private meetings, and a public insistence that the Commonwealth's institutions will hold. This wins no votes and solves nothing material, but relations with the Golds and the Unionists improve[? if marcher_in_government:, and the cabinet holds together a little better for it?].

@prepare_instability
title: Prepare for internal instability.
subtitle: -1 resources. Recruit quietly for the Banners.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; crisis_urgency += 1; banner_strength += 200; left_dissent -= 3

We set the party's organisers to work while the labour market is slack, and the Banners take in men who have nothing else to do this winter. This is recruitment, not armament. There is no drilling and there are no weapons, and nothing the propertied parties can point to in the Assembly, but Banner strength rises and our Left is satisfied.

@emergency_controls
title: Apply emergency economic controls!
subtitle: The ministries we hold can act now, whatever the Assembly decides.
view-if: chancellor_party == "Marcher" or economic_minister_party == "Marcher" or finance_minister_party == "Marcher"
on-arrival: crisis_urgency += 1; budget += 2; gold_relation -= 6; lvp_relation -= 6; gold_right += 1; lvp_right += 1; collectivist_relation += 5*(1-dissent); left_dissent -= 10; left_strength += 2; economy_goal_marcher += 1

We use the ministries we hold rather than wait for the Assembly: controls on credit and currency, emergency powers over the exchanges, and restrictions on what the great houses may do with their money while the country goes hungry. The Treasury's position improves at once.

The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> are appalled. This is exactly the confiscatory instinct they warn their donors about, and relations with them fall. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> note with some surprise that we were willing to do it, and relations with them improve. Our own Left is pleased for the first time in months.
